    "text": "Se H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de \u00feus to his halgum apostolum, her on \u00feisum life libbende mid mannum, for \u00f0on \u00fee he oft\nBet\u00e6c \u00feine wican; ne miht \u00feu beon leng on minum folgo\u00fee.\nAnd se gerefa \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his agenum mode, Hw\u00e6t m\u00e6g ic la nu don?\nNu ic beo bescired, and ic sylf ne m\u00e6g mid minum fotum delfan, ne ic ne m\u00e6g for sceame ahw\u00e6r\nAnd he eft \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic wylle nu betwyx \u00feisum tilian me freonda on \u00feam \u00fee aht sceolon minum\nHe gela\u00f0ode \u00fea sona his under\u00feeoddan him to, \u00fea \u00fee aht sceoldon his hlaforde on feo, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde syllan his hlaforde hundteontig oman mid ele ametene.\n\u00dea het se gerefa him awritan fiftig.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to o\u00f0rum, Hw\u00e6t scealt \u00feu \u00feinum hlaforde?\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde him hundteontig mittan hw\u00e6tes.\nAnd se gerefa het him on gewrite settan \u00fe\u00e6t he hundeahtatig him agifan sceolde.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea heora hlaford herode eft sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feone gerefan on his unrihtwisnysse, for \u00f0an \u00fee he snotorlice\n\u00dea s\u00e6de se H\u00e6lend eft sy\u00f0\u00f0an him \u00feus to: Wyrca\u00f0 eow freonda of \u00f0am unrihtan welan, \u00fe\u00e6t hy\nSe welega man \u00fee h\u00e6fde \u00feone tungerefan is se \u00e6lmihtiga God, \u00fee ah ealle \u00feing, and he bet\u00e6hte\nWe synd his gerefan, \u00fee his welan habba\u00f0, and we yfele aspenda\u00f0 his \u00e6hta him fram, \u00feonne we ure\nBe \u00feam sang se sealmwyrhta, \u00feus secgende us: Homo, cum in honore esset, non intellexit, et cetera: Se\n\u00c6lc \u00feara manna \u00fee his andgit awent to yfelum weorcum fram rihtwisnysse, and nele understandan his\n\u00deas syndan \u00fea leahtras \u00fee mislicia\u00f0 Gode: eawbryce and forliger, and \u00e6lces cynnes reaflac, mor\u00f0d\u00e6da\nVton nu geedl\u00e6can, \u00fe\u00e6t is, eft eow nu secgan, \u00feisses godspelles anginn, swa swa we \u00e6r s\u00e6don, \u00fe\u00e6t ge\nBet\u00e6c \u00feine wican; ne miht \u00feu beon leng on minum folgo\u00f0e.\nOn twa wisan us gelanga\u00f0 and him to clypa\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend, o\u00f0\u00f0e on andweardum life \u00e6rest to d\u00e6dbote,\nNu sceole we be\u00f0encan us sylfe her on life, \u00fe\u00e6t we to yfele ne beon eft on \u00f0am dome.\nAnd se gerefa \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his agenum mode, Hw\u00e6t m\u00e6g ic la nu don, nu ic beo bescired, and ic sylf ne\nWe ne magon delfan, ne we ne moton wyrcan nane gode w\u00e6stmas \u00e6nigre drohtnunge \u00e6fter \u00feisum\nBe \u00f0am ylcan gecw\u00e6\u00f0 eft Godes wisdom: For \u00fe\u00e6s wintres cyle nolde se asolcena erian; he bedeca\u00f0\n\u00de\u00e6t is, \u00fe\u00e6t he on life lytel swanc for Criste, and he \u00f0a ecan myrh\u00fee ne m\u00e6g \u00feonne abiddan.\nHe eft \u00fea sy\u00f0\u00f0an gecw\u00e6\u00f0 on his agenum ge\u00f0ance, Ic wylle nu betwyx \u00feisum tilian me freonda on \u00f0am\nHe gela\u00f0ode \u00fea sona his under\u00feeoddan him to, \u00fea \u00f0e aht sceoldon his hlaforde on feo, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde syllan his hlaforde hundteontig oman mid ele ametene.\n\u00dea het se gerefa him awritan fiftig.\nEle wyxt on treowum, eall swa win de\u00f0; ac \u00fea elebeamas beo\u00f0 maran on w\u00e6stme, and \u00fea berian\nMan de\u00f0 hine to leohte eac on \u00f0am lande on f\u00e6gerum leohtfatum, for \u00f0an \u00fee he f\u00e6t is, and\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to o\u00f0rum, Hw\u00e6t scealt \u00feu \u00feinum hlaforde?\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde him hundteontig mittan hw\u00e6tes; and se gerefa het him on gewrite settan \u00fe\u00e6t\nHe lissode \u00feam mannum \u00fe\u00e6t he mihte hopian to heora freondr\u00e6dene, \u00fe\u00e6t hy underfengon hine eft\nNe sceole we na mid facne us freond gewyrcan, ac \u00feis is so\u00f0 bysen hu we sceolon don of rihtum\n\u00c6lc man sceal don her be his agenre m\u00e6\u00f0e; se \u00fee mare h\u00e6bbe, do be his m\u00e6\u00f0e; se \u00f0e l\u00e6sse h\u00e6bbe, do\nBe \u00f0am cw\u00e6\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend on o\u00ferum godspelle, Gela\u00f0a to \u00feinum godum \u00feearfan and wannhale, blinde\n\u00de\u00e6t is on Domesd\u00e6ge, \u00feonne we of dea\u00f0e arisa\u00f0.\nZacheus se rica w\u00e6s unrihtwis \u00e6t fruman, ac sy\u00f0\u00f0an he underfeng \u00feone fyrmestan cuman, \u00feone\n\u00dea s\u00e6de Zacheus, Drihten leof, ic wylle d\u00e6lan mine \u00e6hta, \u00feone healfan d\u00e6l \u00feearfum, and \u00fe\u00e6rtoeacan\nAnd se H\u00e6lend \u00fea s\u00e6de sona him to andsware, Nu tod\u00e6g is geworden h\u00e6l \u00feisum hirede; for \u00fean \u00fee\nCristes apostolas, swa swa us cy\u00fea\u00f0 bec, forleton heora \u00e6hta ealle for Criste, and him swa folgodon\nSum earm wudewe wearp \u00e6nne feor\u00f0ling betwux o\u00f0rum mannum \u00fee wurpon heora \u00e6lmyssan to \u00f0am\nSe H\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0 eac, Gif hwa syl\u00f0 drincan anum \u00feurstigum men huru ceald w\u00e6ter, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6f\u00f0 his\n\u00deus we sceolon geearnian \u00fea upplican wununge mid \u00feyllicum d\u00e6dum, urum Drihtne to lofe, mid\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea heora hlaford herode eft sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feone gerefan on his unrihtwisnysse, for \u00f0an \u00fee he snotorlice\nVre drihten hera\u00f0 mid beteran herunge his getreowan wicnere, \u00fee his willan gefremode on \u00f0am\n\u00dea worldmen so\u00f0lice, \u00feissere worlde bearn, syndon micele snoteran on heora cynryne \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00dea worldmen cunnon \u00fea worldcundan snoternysse, and \u00fea yfelan hocas \u00fee se H\u00e6lend onscuna\u00f0, be\n\u00deu telest to wisdome \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu \u00fein gewill h\u00e6bbe, and \u00feu m\u00e6ge oferdrifan o\u00feerne man mid wo; ac Crist\nSeo n\u00e6ddre is eallra nytena snoterost, and se deofol \u00feurh hy beswac \u00fea frumsceapenan men; nu sceole\nSeo n\u00e6ddre awurp\u00f0 \u00e6lce geare hire ealdan haman, and bi\u00f0 \u00feonne befangen mid eallniwum felle; uton\nSeo n\u00e6ddre wyle eac bewerian hire heafod, and hy ealle bewindan on embhwyrfte \u00fe\u00e6s heafdes, \u00fe\u00e6t\nSwa we sceolon eac don, gif we snotere beo\u00f0, ne l\u00e6tan us nan \u00feing swa leof swa urne H\u00e6lend, \u00fee is\nCulfre is swi\u00f0e bylewit, and eall butan geallan, and lufa\u00f0 annysse betwyx hyre geferum, and swi\u00f0e\nHealdan we \u00feas \u00feeawas, \u00fe\u00e6t we unhearmgeorne beon, and butan byternysse betwux gebro\u00f0rum\n\u00dea s\u00e6de se H\u00e6lend eft sy\u00f0\u00f0an hym \u00feus to: Wyrca\u00f0 eow freonda of \u00f0am unrihtan welan, \u00fe\u00e6t hy\n\u00dea unrihtan welan syndon witodlice \u00fe\u00e6t weoruldlice feoh, on \u00f0am \u00fea unrihtwisan menn besetta\u00f0 heora\nSe \u00fee \u00e6lmyssan d\u00e6le\u00f0 of \u00f0am eor\u00f0licum feo, and of \u00feam sceortum welum \u00feissere worulde, Godes\nEalswa \u00fea lareowas \u00fee l\u00e6ra\u00f0 Godes folc, and manega gebeta\u00f0 mid heora gebysnungum, magon witan\nSe H\u00e6lend sylf s\u00e6de on sumere o\u00f0re stowe, Se \u00f0e on lytlum \u00feinge bi\u00f0 his hlaforde getrywe, se bi\u00f0\nLytel \u00feing is geteald \u00feises lifes ryne wi\u00f0 \u00f0a ecan worulde, \u00fee ne wur\u00f0 na geendod.\n\u00dea woruldcundan \u00feing syndon witodlice l\u00e6ssan \u00feonne \u00fea gastlican, \u00fee is Godes sylfes lar, \u00fe\u00e6t is se\nSe \u00f0e on woruld\u00feingum wur\u00f0 ungetrywe, ne wur\u00f0 he on \u00feam gastlicum Gode getrywe, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0a\nGetrywsige us se H\u00e6lend \u00feurh \u00feone Halgan Gast, \u00fe\u00e6t we his willan gewyrcan moton; \u00feam sy a",
